When you look in the window, you see a poor starving woodcutter and his wife.	你從窗戶望進去，看見一個貧窮挨餓的樵夫和他的妻子。
You see the woodcutter feeding his poor wife.  Some of the color seems to have come back into her cheeks.	你看見樵夫正在餵他可憐的妻子吃東西，她的臉頰似乎稍微恢復了血色。
There is a window on the back of the house.	房屋後面有一扇窗戶。
There might be someone home.	家裡似乎有人在。
You are in a gloomy forest clearing.	你身處一片陰暗的森林空地。
This lovely meadow is split by a wild, raging river.	這片美麗的草原被一條奔騰洶湧的河流一分為二。
There is a mushroom in the meadow on the other side of the raging river.	洶湧河流的對岸草原上有一朵蘑菇。
There is a large mushroom in the meadow next to the river.	河邊的草原上有一朵大蘑菇。
There is a large mushroom growing in the ground close by.	附近的地上長著一朵大蘑菇。
There is nothing of interest around you.	你四周沒有什麼值得注意的東西。
You see the familiar side of the raging river.	你看見這條洶湧河流你熟悉的這一岸。
The land across the river looks enchanting.  You wonder how you can get there.	河對岸的土地看起來迷人極了，你不禁想著該怎麼過去。
It would be too dangerous to try and jump from boulder to boulder.	想從一顆巨石跳到另一顆巨石實在太危險了。
The swiftly-moving water looks dangerous.	湍急的水流看起來很危險。
You hold the mushroom up to your nose and inhale the fragrance. It smells just like a fresh-picked mushroom should.	你把蘑菇舉到鼻子前聞了聞，聞起來就像剛採下的新鮮蘑菇一樣。
You can just detect the aroma of fresh mushroom.	你隱約聞到新鮮蘑菇的香氣。
Yes, there's a definite mushroom tang in the air.	沒錯，空氣中確實帶著蘑菇的氣味。
You've already picked it.	你已經摘過了。
The mushroom is on the far side of the river.	蘑菇在河的對岸。
You can't pick the mushroom while you're invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法摘蘑菇。
Far in the distance, you can see the spires and turrets of King Edward's castle.	遠方，你能看見愛德華國王城堡的尖塔與角樓。
You don't have the mushroom anymore.	你身上已經沒有蘑菇了。
A large bulbous mushroom grows in the distance.	遠處長著一朵碩大渾圓的蘑菇。
This is a small, aromatic mushroom.	這是一朵小巧芳香的蘑菇。
The rampaging river roils around the rough rocks.	狂暴的河水在嶙峋的岩石間翻騰。
The water is swiftly flowing around the rock.	河水湍急地繞著岩石流過。
The water cascades down a small waterfall here.	河水在這裡形成一道小瀑布傾瀉而下。
You need to be closer to do that.	你得靠近一點才能這麼做。
The face of the cliff is too steep for you to climb.	這面峭壁太陡了，你爬不上去。
In the depths of the large hole you seem to sense a faint, green glow.	在這個大洞的深處，你似乎察覺到一絲微弱的綠光。
Don't be afraid... get closer.	別害怕……靠近一點。
There is a hole in this part of the meadow.	這片草原上有一個洞。
Beautiful spring flowers ring the meadow.	美麗的春花環繞著這片草原。
The meadow is bounded by a steep cliff. There is a deep hole in the ground.	這片草原以一面陡峭的懸崖為界，地上還有一個很深的洞。
Off in the distance, you can see the beautiful snow-capped mountains of Daventry.	遠方，你能看見戴凡確王國美麗的雪山。
As you struggle to retain your balance, the magic ring slips from your finger and vanishes.	你奮力想保持平衡時，魔戒從你的手指上滑落，消失無蹤。
There is no need to throw the dagger, there are no enemies here.	沒必要投擲短刀，這裡沒有敵人。
You can't climb down the rope any farther.	你沒辦法再順著繩索往下爬了。
You are as far down as you'll get without being in the water.	不下水的話，你已經爬到能到的最低處了。
You can't climb down while swimming.	你游泳時沒辦法往下爬。
There's no point in becoming invisible here; the well is dark enough as it is.	在這裡隱形沒有意義，這口井本來就夠暗了。
You're frantically swimming in the cold water of the well	你正在井裡冰冷的水中拚命游著
You're suspended in a bucket above the cold water below.	你懸掛在水桶裡，位於下方冰冷的井水之上。
You are hanging on a rope, above the cold well water below.	你吊掛在繩索上，位於下方冰冷的井水之上。
You can just see the opening of the well above you.	你隱約能看見上方井口的開口。
You can barely see the bottom of the well.	你幾乎看不清井底。
You see the well water below you.	你看見下方的井水。
You are sitting in the bucket.	你坐在水桶裡。
Algae and lichen cover the damp well walls.	潮濕的井壁上覆滿了藻類與地衣。
There is no reason to stop swimming.  You may drown.	沒有理由停止游泳，你可能會淹死。
You cannot stop something you haven't started.	你沒辦法停止一件根本還沒開始的事。
You already are swimming.	你已經在游泳了。
You have to be swimming before you can go diving.	你得先游泳，才能潛水。
You're too busy drowning right now.	你現在正忙著淹死，沒空做別的事。
You can't climb up the wall from there.	你沒辦法從那裡爬上牆。
There is no rope here.	這裡沒有繩索。
Leave the rope where it is; you may find a use for it later.	讓繩索留在原地，你之後也許用得上。
You leap out of the water and grab the rope.	你從水裡一躍而起，抓住繩索。
You're too busy drowning at the moment.	你現在正忙著淹死，沒空做別的事。
You can't climb up the rope from there.	你沒辦法從那裡爬上繩索。
You don't have a dagger.	你身上沒有短刀。
You can't cut the rope from here.	你沒辦法從這裡切斷繩索。
You're already sitting in the bucket.	你已經坐在水桶裡了。
You leap out of the water and climb into the bucket.	你從水裡一躍而起，爬進水桶裡。
There's no point in sitting in there.	坐進去沒有意義。
Jumping into the bucket is not only pointless, it's dangerous.	跳進水桶不僅沒有意義，還很危險。
It's too late for that.  You'll never get into the bucket now.	太遲了，你現在已經進不了水桶了。
There is no bucket here.	這裡沒有水桶。
Just jump into the water if you like.	你想的話，儘管跳進水裡吧。
You're busy drowning at the moment.	你現在正忙著淹死，沒空做別的事。
You drink all the water in the bucket.  You must have been thirsty!	你把水桶裡的水全喝光了，看來你一定是渴壞了！
You open your mouth and swallow some water.	你張開嘴巴，吞了幾口水。
It's hard to jump without solid ground under your feet.	腳下沒有堅實的地面，很難跳起來。
You are not in the bucket.	你不在水桶裡。
Jumping will take you where you want to go.	跳下去就能帶你到你想去的地方。
You have taken the bucket already.	你已經拿走水桶了。
You manage to take the bucket.	你成功拿到了水桶。
It would be easier if the bucket wasn't attached to the rope.	要是水桶沒綁在繩索上，事情會容易得多。
This weathered old bucket has withstood many years of use.	這只飽經風霜的舊水桶，已經耐用了許多年。
The rope is thick and sturdy; it can easily support many times your weight.	這條繩索又粗又堅固，輕輕鬆鬆就能承受好幾倍你的體重。
Though you try, the fall has knocked the wind out of you, and your lungs quickly fill with water.	儘管你努力掙扎，這一摔已經讓你喘不過氣，肺裡很快就灌滿了水。
You have taken the only bucket.	你已經拿走了唯一的水桶。
There's no bucket here.	這裡沒有水桶。
You're climbing a rope, suspended inside a dark, damp well.	你正攀著繩索，懸在一口陰暗潮濕的井裡。
The old rope extends into the sunlight far above you.	這條老舊的繩索一路延伸到你頭頂上方的陽光裡。
Below you, you see the well's cold, dark water.	在你下方，你看見井裡陰暗冰冷的水。
Just below you, there's an old, weathered bucket.	就在你下方，有一只飽經風霜的舊水桶。
You can't stand at the moment.	你現在沒辦法站起來。
The bucket in which you're sitting is suspended a short distance above the well's cold, dark water.	你坐著的這只水桶，懸在井裡陰暗冰冷的水面上方不遠處。
You're sitting in a bucket, suspended inside a dark, damp well.	你坐在水桶裡，懸在一口陰暗潮濕的井裡。
You'll have to be holding the bucket first.	你得先抓住水桶才行。
Unfortunately, the walls of the well are too slick and slimy to be climbed.	可惜井壁又滑又黏，沒辦法攀爬。
When the goat saw how dark it was in here, it decided not to stay around.	山羊一看這裡有多暗，就決定不留在這裡了。
The cave walls are hewn from the living rock of the mountain.  They're dark, cold, and covered with a thin layer of slime.	洞穴的牆壁是從山體的岩床鑿刻而成，陰暗冰冷，還覆著一層薄薄的黏液。
It is a huge piece of granite.	這是一大塊花崗岩。
This is a large, apparently vacant cave.  Damp and cool, the cave is lit only by the sunlight streaming in through the cave's entrance to the west.	這是一個空曠寬敞的洞穴，似乎空無一物，陰涼潮濕，唯一的光源是從西邊洞口灑進來的陽光。
A large boulder is blocking what may be another entrance to this cave.	一塊巨石擋住了這個洞穴另一個可能的入口。
It took millenniums for these stalagmites and stalactites to form.	這些石筍與鐘乳石經過了千萬年才形成。
Looking out the cave opening, you are able to admire the beautiful scenery outside.	望向洞口，你能欣賞到外頭美麗的景色。
It leads to another portion of the cave.	它通往洞穴的另一個區域。
This opening is blocked by a large boulder.	這個洞口被一塊巨石擋住了。
It is on the far side of the cave.	它在洞穴的另一端。
It is far too heavy to carry around.	它太重了，帶不走。
You need to move closer to try that.	你得再靠近一點才能試試看。
It is impossible for you to move a boulder this large.	你不可能搬得動這麼大的一塊巨石。
Yeech.  Fear not, you won't need it.	呃……別擔心，你用不到它。
There is nothing of interest on top of the boulder.	巨石上面沒有什麼值得注意的東西。
The brackish water would not be too satisfying.  It may even make you sick.	這種帶鹹味的濁水喝起來不會怎麼可口，說不定還會讓你生病。
Drops of brackish water fall from the stalactites.	鐘乳石上滴落著帶鹹味的濁水。
Small puddles of water, acrid and unpleasant, collect beneath the dripping rock formations above.	上方滴水的岩層下方積著一灘灘刺鼻難聞的水窪。
The bucket doesn't have water in it.	水桶裡沒有水。
The dragon is dead.  His fire can no longer harm you.	巨龍已經死了，牠的火焰再也傷不了你。
You have already doused the dragon's fire.  It has crept off in embarrassment!	你已經澆熄了巨龍的火焰，牠尷尬地悄悄溜走了！
Maybe you should try that from a different spot.	也許你該換個地方試試看。
This boulder is a huge chunk of granite.	這塊巨石是一大塊花崗岩。
In this large underground cavern, there is one slimy green dead dragon, an opening on one side, and a very large boulder.	在這個寬闊的地底洞穴裡，有一條渾身黏液的綠色巨龍已死，一側有個洞口，還有一塊碩大的巨石。
There is a dead dragon, a large boulder, and a seemingly ordinary mirror in the cave.	洞穴裡有一條死去的巨龍、一塊巨石，還有一面看似平凡無奇的鏡子。
The cavern is empty, save for a couple of openings on either side.	這個洞穴空無一物，只有兩側各有一個洞口。
There is a large granite boulder in the cave, as well as a mirror...a MAGIC mirror!!	洞穴裡有一塊巨大的花崗岩巨石，還有一面鏡子……一面「魔鏡」！！
In this large underground cavern, there is a ferocious fire-breathing dragon, an opening on one side, and a very large boulder.	在這個寬闊的地底洞穴裡，有一條兇猛的噴火巨龍，一側有個洞口，還有一塊碩大的巨石。
The ferocious fire-breathing dragon is protecting the magic mirror.	這條兇猛的噴火巨龍正守護著魔鏡。
Parts of the cave are made impassable by huge, jagged stalagmites.  The craggy limestone stalactites hang menacingly from the roof of the cavern.  It took millenniums for these stalagmites and stalactites to form.	洞穴的部分區域被巨大嶙峋的石筍擋住，無法通行。嶙峋的石灰岩鐘乳石從洞頂陰森森地垂掛而下。這些石筍與鐘乳石經過了千萬年才形成。
The hole seems to lead further into the cave.	這個洞似乎通往洞穴更深處。
The faint images of reflected light issue from the entrance.	微弱的反射光影從入口透出。
There are two entrances to the cave.	這個洞穴有兩個入口。
In this large cavern, there is a slimy dead dragon.	在這個寬闊的洞穴裡，有一條渾身黏液的死去巨龍。
The dragon has fled, never to return.	巨龍已經逃走，再也不會回來了。
The dragon's rough, red pointed tongue protrudes awkwardly from the dead dragon's maw.	死去巨龍的嘴裡，粗糙的紅色尖舌尷尬地伸出口外。
The dragon's still got it.	巨龍依然留著它。
It would be easier if the dragon wasn't using it.	要是巨龍沒在用它，事情會容易得多。
